There are three R files to fit the models from Section 6 of the manuscript using adaptive Gibbs sampling:
* multiprobitregr.R: use to fit the multivariate probit regression model with structured matrix-t prior to the Finnish birds data (see Section 6.2 of the manuscript).
* hourlygasdemand.R: use to fit the stationary dynamic factor model with structured matrix-normal prior to the hourly gas demand data (see Section 6.3 of the manuscript).
* commonfunctions.R: sourced by other two .R files and contains functions common to both.

There are two Stan programs to fit the models from Section 6 of the manuscript using (non-adaptive) Hamiltonian Monte Carlo via Stan:
* multiprobitregr.stan: use to fit the multivariate probit regression model with structured matrix-t prior to the Finnish birds data (see Section 6.2 of the manuscript).
* hourlygasdemand.stan: use to fit the stationary dynamic factor model with structured matrix-normal prior to the hourly gas demand data (see Section 6.3 of the manuscript).

